#: KrohnkiteConfigForm%23292
msgid ""
"<html><head/><body><p>Overriding default parameters for the specified "
"WindowClass. Format:</p><p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">WindowClass</"
"span><span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" "
"font-weight:700;\">SpecialFlag,SpecialFlag...</span><span style=\" font-"
"weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">"
"shortname=value,shortname=value...&lt;Enter&gt;</span></p><p>format with "
"specified titlе, you can specify only part of the title by writing it in "
"square brackets:</p><p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">WindowClass</span>"
"<span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-"
"weight:700;\">Title</span><span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">"
":</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">SpecialFlag,SpecialFlag...</span>"
"<span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-"
"weight:700;\">shortname=value,shortname=value...&lt;Enter&gt;</span></p><p>"
"<span style=\" font-weight:700;\">pin - </span>docked window with this flag "
"will displace another if their positions are equal.</p><p><span style=\" "
"font-weight:700;\">left,right,top,bottom</span> - you can use one them to "
"explicitly set the initial position.</p><p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">"
"auto</span> - automatically makes a window docked. Krohnkite version "
"&gt;=0.9.9.1</p><p>You can only write down the parameters you want to "
"change. You can see the short name of the parameter if you hover over any "
"default parameter above.</p><p>Examples:</p><p>1. if Elisa switches to dock "
"it will have higher priority, top dock position and 10% of screen height </p>"
"<p>org.kde.elisa<span style=\" font-weight:700;\">:pin,top:hh=10</span></p>"
"<p>2. Conky automatic docking:     <span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-"
"weight:700;\">Conky</span><span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">"
":</span><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-weight:700;\">auto</span>"
"<span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-"
"family:'Hack'; font-weight:700;\"/></p><p><span style=\" font-"
"family:'Hack';\">3.With title specified: </span><span style=\" font-"
"weight:700;\">com.obsproject.Studio</span><span style=\" font-weight:700; "
"color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">Scripts</span>"
"<span style=\" font-weight:700; color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-"
"weight:700;\">auto,left</span><span style=\" font-weight:700; "
"color:#ff0000;\">:</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">vw=50</span></p></"
"body></html>"
msgstr ""

#: KrohnkiteConfigForm%23293
msgid ""
"<html><head/><body><p><span style=\" font-size:12pt;\">Overriding default "
"parameters for every surface. Format: </span><span style=\" font-size:12pt; "
"font-weight:700;\">"
"OuputName:ActivityId:VirtualDesktopName:shortname=value,shortname=value... "
"&lt;Enter&gt;</span></p><p><span style=\" font-size:12pt;\">You can only "
"write down parameters you want to change. You can see the short name of the "
"parameter if you hover over any default parameter above.</span></p><p><span "
"style=\" font-size:12pt;\">Next example override three params on all "
"surfaces with OutputName=HDMI-A-1 </span></p><p><span style=\" font-"
"size:12pt; font-weight:700;\">HDMI-A-1:::hh=80,vw=80,ha=left</span></p><p>"
"<span style=\" font-size:12pt;\">this one, will override two params only for "
"defined display, virtual desktop and activity</span></p><p><span style=\" "
"font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;\">HDMI-A-1:99e10d31-e8f3-44aa-bbed-"
"2a543f13fa54:Desktop 1:vg=5,va=2</span></p></body></html>"
msgstr ""

