#: KrohnkiteConfigForm%23352
msgid ""
"<html><head/><body><p><span style=\" font-size:11pt;\">Also, in addition to "
"the fact that you can include only the modules you need, you can enable </"
"span><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-size:11pt;\">Filter</span><span "
"style=\" font-size:11pt;\"> checkbox and use other filters in filter line "
"edit:</span></p><p><span style=\" font-size:11pt;\">- </span><span style=\" "
"font-size:11pt; font-weight:700;\">winclass</span></p><p><span style=\" font-"
"size:11pt;\">Examples:</span></p><p><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-"
"size:11pt;\">- </span><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-size:11pt; "
"font-weight:700;\">winclass=[konsole]</span><span style=\" font-size:11pt; "
"font-weight:700;\"/><span style=\" font-size:11pt;\">- some modules may be "
"filtered by a window class, so this logs modules will show only windows with "
"class that contains </span><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-"
"size:11pt;\">konsole</span><span style=\" font-size:11pt;\"> word.</span></p>"
"<p><span style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-size:11pt;\">- </span><span "
"style=\" font-family:'Hack'; font-size:11pt; font-weight:700;\">"
"!winclass=org.kde.elisa:org.kde.ruler</span><span style=\" font-"
"size:11pt;\"> -Exclude Elisa and Kruler from log output</span></p></body></"
"html>"
